      }
    }
  ],
  "tables": [],
  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "To comply with regulatory requirements, you sometimes need to provide information and supporting documentation in the form of declarations about the types of encryption used by your app. The app encryption declarations resource represents this information, and enables you to:",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "> **Note**\n>\n>  Builds that have the `usesNonExemptEncryption` flag set to true in the app’s property list must link to an app encryption declaration before the app can be submitted for beta app review.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "For more information, see `https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-app-information/overview-of-export-compliance`.",
          "refs": [
            "https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-app-information/overview-of-export-compliance"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "listItems": [
        {
          "text": "View information about the declaration, and",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Assign the declaration to a build.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Create app encryption declarations in App Store Connect.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Upload app encryption declaration documents.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
